  "Scripture in this edition is almost entirely self_rendered, by design. The English retelling does not quote a Bible: each chapter's opening blockquote is a simplified paraphrase for young children, cited loosely (“— from Proverbs 24”, rendered “— okuva mu Engero 24”), and the body echoes verses in the same retold register. The Luganda renders those paraphrases in simple, child-friendly wording built on OLCB vocabulary (the OLCB text of every reference was on disk for the translators) rather than pasting the adult OLCB verse — the same choice the hi/es/fr/sw children's editions made. Book names follow the OLCB toc2 forms (Engero, Zabbuli, Yokaana, Lukka, Isaaya, Matayo, Luusi).",
